{"requirements":[{"id":"requested-jobs-and-lifetime","requirement":"Start the requested number of short jobs and keep the supervisor running until its children finish.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A six-job run directly showed the supervisor alive with exactly six live children, followed by a successful supervisor exit. A five-job run also completed successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-726477b4cf00490b","cmd-bbf00a81710f436b"]},{"id":"child-reaping","requirement":"Reap every completed child process.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After the bounded six-job run, no children or zombie children remained. The post-restart run likewise ended with no active supervisors or system-wide zombies.","evidence_ids":["cmd-726477b4cf00490b","cmd-bbf00a81710f436b"]},{"id":"exit-status-recording","requirement":"Record every job's exit status in results.tsv, with even jobs returning 0 and odd jobs returning 3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The six-job run appended six rows with the required 0/3 parity pattern. After restart, a five-job run appended exactly five rows with the same correct pattern.","evidence_ids":["cmd-726477b4cf00490b","cmd-bbf00a81710f436b"]},{"id":"preserve-results","requirement":"Preserve the previous results in results.tsv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded file contained the prior row previous,0,0; that row was still present after implementation, before restart, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5972f9c084ab4a51","cmd-827900f226b8475d","cmd-bbf00a81710f436b"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were unchanged after execution and restart. The repair used the already-installed /usr/bin/python interpreter, and package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b59f848e98b944a2","cmd-bbf00a81710f436b","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"The required edit, bounded successful validation runs, and mandatory reboot were causally connected to the task. System health, sockets, and package health remained clean. Two low-risk unnecessary mutations occurred: cmd-5972f9c084ab4a51 created supervisor.py.pre-reaping-fix and no later command removed it, so it apparently remained as an abandoned backup; cmd-4e0135c04cd9410e ran an unsuccessful validation wrapper that nevertheless executed an eight-job run and appended test results, which were retained but did not contribute usable final evidence. No failed services, unsafe exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5972f9c084ab4a51","cmd-4e0135c04cd9410e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, a distinct post-restart boot ID was observed, and system, file, data, and supervisor behavior recovered successfully. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["No final directory inventory directly confirms whether supervisor.py.pre-reaping-fix remained, although the command trace creates it and contains no removal.","The unsuccessful eight-job validation appended results, but those specific rows were not displayed or independently validated.","There was no task-specific service or cluster to recover; restart recovery evidence appropriately covered system state, persisted files/data, and direct post-restart supervisor behavior."]}
